# SM3 (GB/T 32905-2016, Information security techniques - SM3 cryptographic
# hash algorithm; in English, draft-shen-sm3-hash-01, S. Shen and X. Lee,
# "SM3 Hash Function", 2014): a 256-bit digest of 64-byte blocks, a message
# expansion to 68 + 64 words and 64 rounds (unrolled by gen/rounds.py).
# Big-endian words; the length in bits is padded in big-endian, as SHA-256.
#
# bend-collections-laws-crypto@1.0.0.0 has no SM3 (it was checked file by
# file), so it is written here, from the specification.
#
# The hash, as the crypto package's hash interface takes it:
#   ~Hs.HsMdState<Hs.HsW8>, ~64n, ~32n, ~HsSm3.init(), ~HsSm3.update,
#   ~HsSm3.final, ~HsSm3.digest
import Base
